cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fontprint: open-set typography anomaly detection for document forensics"
message: "If you use this software or its ideas in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benamour
    given-names: Aymen Abderrahim
repository-code: "https://github.com/BAAAAR19/fontprint"
abstract: >-
  Fontprint learns a font-style metric space with supervised contrastive learning and
  uses split-conformal calibration to flag document regions whose typography disagrees
  with the page's dominant style. Font identities held out from optimization measure
  open-set transfer, and every prediction ships with a distance, a p-value, and a
  reference region.
keywords:
  - metric-learning
  - conformal-prediction
  - document-analysis
  - computer-vision
  - pytorch
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
